comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T09:58:08.752Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the new sandbox lifecycle regression fails on baseline because a deleted item returns the undifferentiated not-found error. Implementation verifies the retained stream before disclosing deletion and selects the latest materialized version, with explicit legacy compaction handling. Reusing canonical predecessor pm-wdrkfr; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-09-11T10:19:12.053Z","harness:codex","Recovery integration evidence: verified whole-record replay is required before claiming deletion; compacted streams retain durable version offsets and use timestamps only when unambiguous. Missing, restored, unrecoverable and corrupt streams have distinct tested behavior. SDK and human/JSON CLI recovery execute successfully in sandboxed temporary trackers."
  "2026-09-11T10:22:00.914Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance passed in an unrelated temporary project: init, history contracts, parent/child creation, claim, comments/notes/learnings, linked file, deletion, JSON tombstone, exact suggested historical-read execution, restore, and verified history. Six retained materialized versions were recovered with hierarchy and annotations intact. SDK recovery command rendering reuses the same shell-quoting implementation as existing SDK callers."
  "2026-09-11T10:23:18.110Z","harness:codex","Manual-acceptance precision: the successful replay and restore targeted durable version 6 (the latest materialized version), rather than separately restoring all six prior versions. Hierarchy, annotations and linked artifacts survived that exact recovery."
  "2026-09-11T10:28:06.853Z","harness:codex","Full-suite regression found and fixed: a failed Beads import can reserve a history path as a directory while rolling back the item. Tombstone discovery now probes regular stream files only, preserving the existing NOT_FOUND exit for that rollback boundary. All 33 focused tests passed, including the existing Beads regression. Additional negative cases reject deletion claims for a create-only retained stream or an unmaterializable checkpoint."
  "2026-09-11T10:44:17.586Z","harness:codex","Additional TDD integrity boundary: copying a valid history stream under a different item ID incorrectly produced a deleted-item claim before the correction. Recovery now rejects any retained materialized identity that disagrees with the requested subject using history_replay_invalid. The new regression failed before the guard and passes afterward. Direct structured-formatter assertions verify tombstone propagation alongside the real CLI acceptance; all five focused history-contract/recovery tests pass."
  "2026-09-11T10:53:03.043Z","harness:codex","Implementation verification: the final full suite passed all 8713 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero uncovered counts. All four TypeScript projects and both linked recovery/Beads commands passed. The earlier linked failure was a malformed legacy fixture incorrectly passed through the normalizing writer; direct sealed historical data now exercises that boundary faithfully. Subject mismatch, corrupt proof, ambiguous checkpoints, directory stream paths, JSON/human diagnostics and executable recovery are covered. Final static and hosted review gates remain required before merge."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-11T10:29:43.036Z","harness:codex","A deleted-item diagnosis needs verified retained history and a replayable address. A missing file alone, a restored stream, a directory occupying the stream path, or an ambiguous legacy checkpoint timestamp must not imply recoverable deletion."
